  "strategy": "*We must minimize the evaluation function.*  \n256  \nThe fundamental idea: minimize score = 2*n*max(convolve(a,a))/sum(a)**2  \nWe will use a two-level optimization:  \n1. Start with generated sequences (uniform, ramp, parent) and optimize with local search and gradient descent.  \n2. Evaluate and share rankings across smaller/larger lengths within a time budget.  \n*Implementation outline:*  \nWe will allocate time budgets dynamically using a priority list. The highest priority is sequences yielding lowest scores.  \nDefine configs: [('uniform', 256, 'constant'), ('ramp', 256, 'ramp'), ('parent', 256, 'parent')]  \n*Algorithmic core:*  \n- Generate initial sequence for each config to break symmetry (add small random perturbation).  \n- Apply local search (gradient-based) with adaptive step sizes and dimensionality checks.  \n- Run an LP-based optimizer for formal tightening after local search.  \n- Evaluate scores using `evaluate_sequence`: minimal constraints but adequate validity checks.  \n- Keep track of best candidate found and return it if it's valid.  \nWe will schedule configurations by:  \n  1. uniform (fallback, safer than ramp)  \n  2. parent (if available and improves on uniform)  \n  3. ramp  \nThen distribute time according to configs' base requirements, starting from shorter sequences.  \n*Optimization goals:*  \nAll length claims are tentative (<= 1500s):  \n  uniform_512: time=300s (score improvement priority)  \n  If time remains: uniform_1024: 400s, uniform_2048: 500s for very precise results, or shorter versions like uniform_128:  \n  We are cautious of task\u30cf\u30a4\u30d1\u30e9 management.  \n*New key features:*  \n- Gradient-based refinement after random walks.  \n- Progressive tightening via LP_solver.  \n- Hybrid initialization: normal + uniform  \n*Why this should improve:*  \nThe mixed approaches enhance exploration-exploitation trade-off, breaking the routine of previous optimizations. Safety checks and prior data availability (56/ penalty avoidance) are prioritized over pure brute-force.  \n*Terminology:*  \n`evaluate_sequence`: \n  - Is fixed. No reprocessing. \n  - Returns score only after LR, ADMM, and bounds checks.  \n*Caveats:*  \nNone of the global variables (like `parent`) should be referenced except `parent` itself, which holds historical bests.",
